  "_comment": "The indexing queue's tier map (docs/plans/indexing-queue-2026-11-23.md, read by scripts/index-queue.mjs). Paths, never full URLs. t1 is a fixed list; t2/t3 are classes matched by regex, in order; /questions/ is always tier 5 and Google only. A class-2 page is queued at tier 2 only when it is new to the engine (not indexed) or listed under pending; otherwise it ranks as tier 4. pending holds the pages an agent shipped or materially changed: add a line in the same PR as the page, with the PR and the date. A gate holds a pending page until it is true: flag = the key must read true in src/data/feature-flags.js (a missing key is OFF here); liveMarker = the live page must contain this string (checked only with --live). flagGated maps a page that is rendered only behind a flag to that flag: such a page is never queued, on any engine, while the flag is off (and with --live, not before it answers 200). A pending gate only decides when the pending boost applies; with the gate closed the page is ranked by its class rules like any other. skip lists pages never worth a request (legal pages; /weekly/ changes every week by design).",
